ollama for Debian
=================

This package provides ollama, repackaged for Debian-based distributions.
It is built from the upstream ollama project at https://github.com/ollama/ollama.

Package split
-------------

The ollama package is split into multiple packages:

  ollama                  Main program and CLI
  libollama-common        CPU dispatch libraries and Vulkan backend (required)
  libollama-nvidia        NVIDIA CUDA shared libraries
  libollama-amd           AMD ROCm shared libraries

Install the appropriate GPU backend package for your hardware. On systems
with no discrete GPU, libollama-common alone is sufficient for CPU inference.

GPU backend selection
---------------------

  NVIDIA GPUs:  apt install ollama libollama-nvidia
  AMD GPUs:     apt install ollama libollama-amd

Only one GPU backend package should be installed at a time.

Configuration
-------------

The ollama systemd service is installed but not started by default.
To enable and start ollama:

  systemctl enable --now ollama

The service listens on localhost:11434 by default. See the upstream
documentation at https://ollama.com for configuration options.

APT repository
--------------

This package is distributed via a self-hosted APT repository.
To add the repository and install:

  curl -fsSL https://lingfish.github.io/ollama-deb/ | bash
  apt install ollama

The repository provides stable and release candidate (rc) suites.

Reporting issues
----------------

Report packaging issues (not upstream ollama bugs) at:
  https://github.com/lingfish/ollama-deb/issues

For upstream ollama issues, use:
  https://github.com/ollama/ollama/issues

Upgrade notes
-------------

apt-listchanges can show changelog and NEWS entries when upgrading.
Install it for a better upgrade experience:

  apt install apt-listchanges
